# Blog Post: Top 5 Care Coordination Trends for 2026

**Author:** Marketing Team
**Date:** January 8, 2026

As we enter 2026, care coordination continues to evolve rapidly. Here are the top 5 trends we're watching:

## 1. AI-Powered Predictive Analytics

Hospitals are increasingly using AI to predict which patients are at high risk for readmission, allowing for proactive interventions.

## 2. Telehealth Integration

The pandemic accelerated the adoption of telehealth, and now hospitals are looking to integrate telehealth into their care coordination workflows.

## 3. Patient Engagement

Patients want to be more involved in their own care. Tools that facilitate patient communication and engagement are in high demand.

## 4. Interoperability

The ability to seamlessly exchange data between different EHR systems remains a top priority for hospitals.

## 5. Value-Based Care

As healthcare shifts from fee-for-service to value-based care, care coordination becomes even more critical for managing patient populations and improving outcomes.

